  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Gyani Sharma vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 16 October, 2020 Author: Anand Pathak Bench: Anand Pathak High Court Of Madhya Pradesh 1 M.Cr.C.No.24970/2020 (Gyani Sharma Vs. State of M.P. )",
    "facts": "The applicant has filed this fifth bail application u/S.439 Cr.P.C for grant of bail. Applicant has been arrested on 3.9.2019 by Police Station, Jaura, District Morena, in connection with Crime No.504/2019 for the offence punishable under Sections 420, 272, 273 of IPC and Sections 51 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Except fourth application, all applications have been dismissed as withdrawn.",
    "arguments": "It is the submission of learned counsel for the applicant that he is suffering confinement since 3.9.2019 and more than 13 months have passed in confinement and now he learnt the lesson hard way and would mend his ways and would become a better citizen by becoming a law abiding citizen. Looking to the period of custody as well as the fact that some of the witnesses have been examined, his case for bail be considered. He undertakes to cooperate in trial and further undertakes to perform community service and to serve environmental/national/social cause HIGH COURT OF MADHYA PRADESH (Gyani Sharma Vs. State of M.P. ) voluntarily to purge his misdeeds, if any. On behalf of the applicant, learned counsel for the applicant submits that he intends to serve the cause of advocates who are in financial distress by making contribution in the funds of High Court Bar Association, Gwalior, on his own volition. On these premises, he prayed for bail Learned counsel for the State opposed the prayer and submits that applicant was accused of providing adulterated items and allegations against him are having wider ramifications.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is the submission of learned counsel for the applicant that he is suffering confinement since 3.9.2019 and more than 13 months have passed in confinement and now he learnt the lesson hard way and would mend his ways and would become a better citizen by becoming a law abiding citizen. Looking to the period of custody as well as the fact that some of the witnesses have been examined, his case for bail be considered. He undertakes to cooperate in trial and further undertakes to perform community service and to serve environmental/national/social cause HIGH COURT OF MADHYA PRADESH (Gyani Sharma Vs. State of M.P. ) voluntarily to purge his misdeeds, if any. On behalf of the applicant, learned counsel for the applicant submits that he intends to serve the cause of advocates who are in financial distress by making contribution in the funds of High Court Bar Association, Gwalior, on his own volition. On these premises, he prayed for bail Learned counsel for the State opposed the prayer and submits that applicant was accused of providing adulterated items and allegations against him are having wider ramifications.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
